## Standing rules for every phase

- Follow `ic-client/.claude/CLAUDE.md` strictly: no `any`, no `as X` without a justifying comment, explicit `Promise<T>` return types, typed `Error` subclasses (never throw strings), all popups as `Drawer anchor="bottom"` bottom sheets.
- No `@types/jest`: `import { jest } from "@jest/globals"`; always `const m = jest.fn<TReturn, TArgs>()`; **never** annotate `let m: jest.Mock<…>` (breaks `tsc`).
- Reuse before writing new code; port from `ic-pizza-kiosk` including its explanatory comments — do not invent.
- Backend repo is read-only. No backend changes are in scope.
- **Do not commit or push.** Leave all changes in the working tree.
- If a requirement turns out to be ambiguous or depends on something not visible, write `needs-clarification.md` with the exact open questions and STOP. Do not guess, do not invent values, do not silently descope.
